{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JPrzTd6MCGUKQ24VHTm8oQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets).\n\n**Current state**:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — code exists (difftest.go, runner.go in source_code)\n- `pkg/format/` — code exists (color.go, size.go in source_code)\n- `pkg/sys/` — no code exists yet, spec complete\n- `cmd/version/` — no code exists, spec complete (only generation target from uc001-magefiles)\n- No cmd/ utilities have code on the working branch\n\n**Current release**: 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Use cases: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils. Of these, uc002-format and uc004-testutils already have code. uc001-magefiles is excluded by DD7 except for cmd/version. **pkg/sys/ (uc003-sys) is the only foundation package without code.**\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nFollowing P5 (libraries before consumers) and P8 (deterministic ordering), `pkg/sys/` must be built before any `cmd/` utility that needs platform-specific syscalls. The architecture identifies file metadata abstraction (stat/lstat with st_mtimespec/st_mtim and st_blocks divergence) as a core capability needed by `du` (rel01.3) and `ls` (deferred). This is the highest-priority missing piece in release 00.0.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/sys file metadata -- Stat and Lstat platform abstraction\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys/ component description, design decisions, technology choices for golang.org/x/sys)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (full PRD for pkg/sys -- read for exact requirement IDs and field specifications)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml (use case for pkg/sys)\n      - go.mod (verify golang.org/x/sys dependency is declared)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (reference for package style, copyright header, SPDX identifier, and PRD-reference comment conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat.go\n        action: create\n        note: Platform-independent FileMetadata struct and public Stat/Lstat functions\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: Darwin-specific Stat_t field extraction using build tag\n      - path: pkg/sys/stat_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: Linux-specific Stat_t field extraction using build tag\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define an exported FileMetadata struct in pkg/sys/stat.go with platform-independent fields covering the stat metadata that diverges between Darwin and Linux: modification time (time.Time), access time (time.Time), block count (int64), block size (int64), device number (uint64), inode number (uint64), hard link count (uint64), UID (uint32), GID (uint32). This struct abstracts the Stat_t field-name divergence so cmd/ packages never import platform-specific syscall types.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement an exported Stat(path string) (FileMetadata, error) function that calls os.Stat, extracts the underlying *syscall.Stat_t via FileInfo.Sys(), and delegates to an unexported extractMetadata function (defined in platform files) to populate FileMetadata. Return a wrapped error if os.Stat fails or the Sys() type assertion fails.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement an exported Lstat(path string) (FileMetadata, error) function with identical logic to Stat but calling os.Lstat so symlinks are not followed. Reuse the same extractMetadata platform function.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Isolate platform-specific Stat_t field access into stat_darwin.go (//go:build darwin) and stat_linux.go (//go:build linux). Each file implements extractMetadata(*syscall.Stat_t) FileMetadata. On Darwin, read Mtimespec/Atimespec for timestamps. On Linux, read Mtim/Atim. Both platforms read Blocks, Blksize, Dev, Ino, Nlink, Uid, Gid from their respective Stat_t field names.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"stat.go contains no build tags. Only stat_darwin.go and stat_linux.go carry build constraints. stat.go defines the struct and public API; platform files supply extractMetadata.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the copyright header, SPDX license identifier, and PRD-reference comment style established in pkg/format/color.go -- e.g., '// Implements: prd002-sys (RN)' at the package doc comment level.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use the standard library syscall.Stat_t (obtained via FileInfo.Sys()) for field access. Import golang.org/x/sys/unix only if the PRD or go.mod indicates it is needed for fields not available in the standard syscall package.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"FileMetadata struct is exported from package sys with all nine fields listed in R1.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Stat() and Lstat() functions are exported and return (FileMetadata, error). Both compile without errors when building for the current platform.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"stat_darwin.go has //go:build darwin and stat_linux.go has //go:build linux. Neither platform file imports the other's types.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/... passes with no errors on the current platform.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Copyright header, SPDX identifier, and PRD-reference comments are present in all three files, matching the style in pkg/format/color.go.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23015,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23015},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0423d77-5007-4f26-a71a-ec93d0e6aa28","uuid":"172c9dfb-c0a2-47d8-b5f1-f425992762bc"}
